      "reason": "The Methods explicitly lists multiple 'other variables' extracted and defines them (study design, tests, maternal characteristics, severity, delivery mode, sample types, timing, variant, clinical outcomes), satisfying the requirement to list and define variables sought."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10b_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_16",
      "quote": "SARS-CoV-2 predominant variant of concern 20 (as reported by authors, or mapped ... by the dominant variant in the country during the study period using https://covariants.org/). A detailed deduplication process was used to cross check data against other studies published by the same authors or those that included women from the same institutions. We contacted study authors for unpublished information and to query duplication of data.",
      "reason": "The manuscript describes some procedures for handling missing/unclear information (mapping variants using covariants.org, deduplication checks, contacting authors), but does not comprehensively describe explicit assumptions made about missing or unclear study information (for example, imputation rules or how ambiguous data were interpreted), so the reporting is partial."
